WEBVTT

00:07.610 --> 00:12.070
Les Misérables

00:07.610 --> 00:12.070
A Girl Named Cosette

00:08.610 --> 00:11.610
Beyond the wind

00:12.070 --> 00:15.490
The wind blows

00:12.070 --> 00:15.490
Kaze ga fuki nuketeku

00:15.490 --> 00:22.080
over the daisies blooming over the stone pavement

00:15.490 --> 00:22.080
Ishidatami ni saku hinagiku

00:22.080 --> 00:25.630
I held my knees

00:22.080 --> 00:25.630
Hiza wo tsuite

00:25.630 --> 00:31.090
and gazed at the flowers

00:25.630 --> 00:31.090
Jitto mitsumeteta

00:31.090 --> 00:34.840
Far away, very far away

00:31.090 --> 00:34.840
Tooku haruka tooku

00:34.840 --> 00:41.470
A gentle voice is calling me

00:34.840 --> 00:41.470
Watashi wo yobu yasashii koe

00:41.470 --> 00:45.060
Let's go look for it

00:41.470 --> 00:45.060
Sagashii ni yukou

00:45.060 --> 00:50.820
Even if we wander aimlessly

00:45.060 --> 00:50.820
Attemonai keredo

00:50.820 --> 00:55.570
The rain comes down

00:50.820 --> 00:55.570
Doushaburi no ame

00:55.570 --> 01:00.330
on a lonely morning

00:55.570 --> 01:00.330
Hitoribocchi no asa

01:00.330 --> 01:04.870
But look, beyond the clouds

01:00.330 --> 01:04.870
Demo hora kumo no mukou

01:04.870 --> 01:09.460
the sunlight is peering at us

01:04.870 --> 01:09.460
Hizashi ga nozoiteruyo

01:09.460 --> 01:11.840
Wipe away your tears

01:09.460 --> 01:11.840
Namida fuite

01:11.840 --> 01:14.760
Look forward

01:11.840 --> 01:14.760
Mae wo muite

01:14.760 --> 01:19.050
and summon all of your strength

01:14.760 --> 01:19.050
Ashimoto chikara komete

01:19.050 --> 01:21.390
Let's walk

01:19.050 --> 01:21.390
Aruite yukou

01:21.390 --> 01:23.770
I'm sure we will make it

01:21.390 --> 01:23.770
Kitto yukeru

01:23.770 --> 01:31.190
The road, the road, continues on...

01:23.770 --> 01:31.190
Michi wa michi wa tsuzuku yo...

01:31.190 --> 01:34.190
forever...

01:31.190 --> 01:33.610
Dokomademo

02:04.940 --> 02:06.050
Yay!

02:17.960 --> 02:18.700
Cosette...

02:18.870 --> 02:19.770
Mother...

02:21.670 --> 02:22.650
Thank you!

02:23.050 --> 02:23.650
Sure!

02:28.050 --> 02:28.710
There you go!

02:29.300 --> 02:30.910
Mother, this is beautiful!

02:31.350 --> 02:35.580
This is Mother's precious pendant.

02:35.770 --> 02:39.540
I will give it to you when you grow up.

02:41.020 --> 02:42.170
Do you want it?

02:42.190 --> 02:42.670
Yes!

02:46.900 --> 02:48.550
Let's go, Cosette.

02:48.570 --> 02:49.220
Yes!

02:58.080 --> 02:59.520
Mother...

02:59.540 --> 03:01.060
Yes, Cosette?

03:01.080 --> 03:03.690
Where is our new home?

03:03.710 --> 03:06.400
We're going to go look for it now.

03:06.420 --> 03:07.190
Really?

03:07.510 --> 03:12.070
Let's find a home where the two of us can live happily, all right?

03:12.340 --> 03:12.910
Yes!

03:18.510 --> 03:23.510
Fantine and Cosette

03:24.190 --> 03:28.470
Montfermeil

03:35.200 --> 03:36.390
Excuse me...

03:36.450 --> 03:40.270
Welcome, we have plenty of fresh fruits and vegetables!

03:40.540 --> 03:43.980
Um... might you have any job openings?

03:44.000 --> 03:45.520
What?

03:45.880 --> 03:48.730
I'm looking for work.
If possible, a live-in position.

03:48.760 --> 03:52.110
I'm in no position to hire someone right now.

03:53.220 --> 03:54.160
I see...

03:54.470 --> 03:55.410
I'm sorry.

04:02.810 --> 04:04.620
Mother, are you angry?

04:06.570 --> 04:10.960
No, I'm fine, Cosette.
Thank you for worrying.

04:10.990 --> 04:11.840
Sure.

04:11.860 --> 04:14.590
Let's go find our new home.

04:14.610 --> 04:15.180
Yes!

04:23.330 --> 04:24.270
Welcome!

04:24.670 --> 04:28.860
Excuse me, I am looking for work.

04:29.420 --> 04:32.400
Do you have any tailoring experience?

04:32.630 --> 04:35.610
Yes, I was a seamstress in Paris.

04:35.890 --> 04:39.530
In Paris, you say?
In that case, you can start right away!

04:40.100 --> 04:40.990
Come on in.

04:41.020 --> 04:42.200
Thank you!

04:42.560 --> 04:43.470
Come inside, Cosette.

04:46.400 --> 04:47.750
Just a minute...

04:49.110 --> 04:51.550
I'm sorry, I didn't know you had a child...

04:51.570 --> 04:52.590
Well...

04:53.030 --> 04:56.650
I'm sorry, we cant hire someone who has a child.

04:56.870 --> 04:59.220
But, I need to find work.

04:59.870 --> 05:00.720
I'm sorry.

05:03.250 --> 05:04.390
Sorry to have bothered you.

05:05.670 --> 05:06.230
Let's go.

05:06.460 --> 05:07.100
All right.

05:15.630 --> 05:16.610
Mother...

05:17.550 --> 05:18.880
I'm hungry.

05:18.890 --> 05:20.120
All right.

05:20.720 --> 05:22.660
Let's go find a baker.

05:22.680 --> 05:23.290
Yes!

05:26.940 --> 05:27.540
Bread!

05:27.560 --> 05:28.830
That's right, Cosette.

05:29.190 --> 05:31.540
This is a baker. Good job finding it.

05:30.550 --> 05:32.750
Bread! They sell bread, right?

05:33.490 --> 05:35.260
Go find a piece that you would like to eat.

05:35.570 --> 05:36.340
Yes!

05:41.240 --> 05:44.140
I'm in no position to hire someone.

05:44.700 --> 05:47.060
I cannot hire someone with a child.

05:51.040 --> 05:52.520
I'm hungry!

05:52.550 --> 05:54.730
Are you by yourself, Little Madame?

05:54.760 --> 05:56.820
No, I'm with Mother.

05:58.050 --> 05:58.700
Mother!

05:59.010 --> 05:59.700
Welcome!

06:00.470 --> 06:02.700
Mother's going to buy me some bread!

06:02.720 --> 06:05.370
How nice! Our bread's delicious, you know!

06:05.850 --> 06:06.720
What will you have?

06:07.810 --> 06:09.710
The smallest piece of bread you have, please.

06:10.060 --> 06:14.060
The smallest would probably be this one...

06:14.070 --> 06:15.920
Wow! It's so small!

06:15.940 --> 06:18.010
Little Madame, are you hungry?

06:18.030 --> 06:18.690
Yes!

06:18.700 --> 06:21.550
In that case, can you eat this much?

06:21.580 --> 06:22.050
Yes!

06:22.490 --> 06:23.510
That's...

06:23.910 --> 06:27.310
They both sell for the same price.

06:27.910 --> 06:29.020
Wow, it's so big!

06:29.040 --> 06:30.410
I see.

06:31.380 --> 06:32.560
Well then, I'll take it.

06:32.960 --> 06:33.980
Thank you!

06:34.500 --> 06:35.360
It smells good!

06:36.050 --> 06:37.190
It's so warm!

06:40.340 --> 06:43.870
Um, do you know of any place that might be hiring around here?

06:46.310 --> 06:50.620
Probably not, the economy's pretty bad these days.

06:51.310 --> 06:53.500
Thank you very much.

06:54.690 --> 06:56.590
I wish I could help.

06:56.900 --> 06:58.340
Let's go, Cosette.

06:58.360 --> 06:59.050
Yes!

06:59.610 --> 07:00.840
Oh, right!

07:01.740 --> 07:04.390
There's a town called Montreuil-Sur-Mer to the north.

07:04.660 --> 07:09.520
They say there's a new factory there that's hiring by the dozens.

07:09.540 --> 07:10.600
Really?

07:10.870 --> 07:12.690
It might just be a rumor, though.

07:14.090 --> 07:16.190
Montreuil-Sur-Mer...

07:17.260 --> 07:20.570
Do you think they'd hire me even if I have a child?

07:20.840 --> 07:24.030
I don't know about that...

07:24.430 --> 07:27.300
But, Montreuil-Sur-Mer's far from here.

07:28.220 --> 07:30.870
It might be a rough journey for the little one.

07:31.980 --> 07:33.000
I see...

07:39.110 --> 07:40.880
Here, Mother, have some.

07:41.820 --> 07:43.840
You're hungry too, aren't you, Mother?

07:44.820 --> 07:46.100
Thank you, Cosette.

07:46.450 --> 07:49.970
But, Mother's all right. Why don't you eat it, Cosette?

07:50.830 --> 07:52.770
If you eat enough, you'll grow real fast.

07:53.210 --> 07:56.190
Yes, I'll get big just like Mother!

07:57.050 --> 07:58.320
Delicious!

07:59.800 --> 08:04.170
<i>Should I go? To Montreuil-Sur-Mer...</i>

08:11.850 --> 08:13.000
I hear children...

08:13.600 --> 08:14.500
I'll go look!

08:14.520 --> 08:15.040
Cosette!

08:19.480 --> 08:20.770
Hello!

08:22.900 --> 08:24.930
Wanna play?

08:25.280 --> 08:25.900
Sure!

08:26.120 --> 08:27.010
Yay!

08:27.030 --> 08:27.720
Cosette!

08:27.740 --> 08:31.140
It's all right. Will you be staying?
Or perhaps, a meal?

08:31.870 --> 08:35.020
No, I'm actually looking for work.

08:35.250 --> 08:37.560
Work? Even though you have a child?

08:37.920 --> 08:38.580
Yes.

08:38.800 --> 08:40.400
Where's her father?

08:41.260 --> 08:42.030
He passed away.

08:43.010 --> 08:48.450
Anyway, there aren't any jobs around here.
Why don't you go look in Paris?

08:48.760 --> 08:49.910
We just came from Paris.

08:51.850 --> 08:56.080
I used to work as a seamstress there, but I was laid off.

08:56.100 --> 09:00.040
I thought that if I left Paris, I could find a live-in job.

09:00.780 --> 09:03.840
I vacated my room and sold all of my furniture.

09:04.780 --> 09:07.220
But I was refused work everywhere I looked because I have a child.

09:07.370 --> 09:09.470
It's impossible to find work with a child.

09:09.490 --> 09:11.640
Why don't you leave your child with us?

09:12.580 --> 09:15.810
If it's all right with you, we'd be happy to look after her.

09:16.920 --> 09:18.620
Husband, what are you saying?!

09:18.880 --> 09:21.480
If you look for work by yourself, someone is bound to hire you right away!

09:21.920 --> 09:25.460
We only ask that you pay for her room and board.

09:25.590 --> 09:28.570
We already raise children of our own, one more wouldn't hurt.

09:28.600 --> 09:29.490
Husband!

09:32.270 --> 09:36.960
Um, thank you for your kindness, but I cannot leave my child.

09:36.980 --> 09:44.380
Think about it! If you find work, you can save some
money and then, one day, live together again.

09:44.400 --> 09:50.220
You two will eventually starve if you're unable to find work.

09:53.580 --> 09:54.810
This is fun!

09:55.080 --> 09:57.640
Azelma wants to ride too!

10:01.130 --> 10:03.540
Azelma wants to ride!

10:03.550 --> 10:05.320
Let Azelma ride!

10:05.630 --> 10:07.110
Just follow my lead...

10:07.430 --> 10:09.240
The poor little thing.

10:10.550 --> 10:12.830
You can rest assured and leave her with us!

10:12.930 --> 10:16.580
We run an inn, after all. We're accustomed to caring for others.

10:16.890 --> 10:23.130
Just look at how well our girls are getting along, they're already like sisters.

10:23.150 --> 10:26.090
But, I think I should probably take Cosette with me.

10:26.650 --> 10:30.680
Isn't a mother's duty to think of her daughter's best interests?

10:31.160 --> 10:33.760
She'll have plenty to eat with us.

10:34.080 --> 10:36.990
Parting with your child is always a sad thing.

10:37.210 --> 10:39.980
As a mother myself, I understand how you feel.

10:40.750 --> 10:44.610
But it's only for a little while, you can come for her real soon!

10:50.890 --> 10:54.780
Um, please look after Cosette.

10:56.470 --> 10:57.370
Please!

10:57.730 --> 10:58.290
Yes!

10:58.560 --> 10:59.470
What are your names?

10:59.480 --> 11:02.250
We're the Thénardiers, what's your name?

11:02.520 --> 11:03.460
I'm Fantine.

11:03.480 --> 11:08.380
I see, Fantine! Leave Cosette to us!

11:08.610 --> 11:12.260
Don't you worry about a thing and work hard!

11:12.280 --> 11:13.470
Thank you!

11:13.740 --> 11:17.530
Well then, let us settle Cosette's room and board in advance.

11:17.540 --> 11:21.270
It's best if we settle this accurately now.

11:22.290 --> 11:23.020
Yes.

11:23.540 --> 11:30.740
Let's see, a month would be about 10 francs, but I'll give you a discount and
make it 7 francs if you pay for 6 months' room and board in advance.

11:31.090 --> 11:34.240
You mentioned that you sold all of your furniture, so you have enough, right?

11:34.640 --> 11:35.990
Yes, I understand.

11:36.220 --> 11:38.040
6 months paid in advance comes to 42 francs.

11:38.350 --> 11:38.910
Yes.

11:38.930 --> 11:43.120
I also request that you leave 15 francs in case of an emergency.

11:43.150 --> 11:45.250
That's 57 francs total.

11:45.360 --> 11:46.040
Yes.

11:46.860 --> 11:47.460
Very well.

11:48.230 --> 11:52.930
This confirms that you have paid 6 month's room and board in advance.

11:53.410 --> 11:54.090
Yes.

11:54.120 --> 11:58.310
That's right! Please leave all of Cosette's clothing and shoes with us.

11:58.330 --> 12:01.730
Yes, I will leave all of Cosette's belongings with you.

12:01.920 --> 12:06.310
Very well! This is all for both of your happiness!

12:06.340 --> 12:13.860
Come back as soon as you can! In the meantime, we'll treat
Cosette just as good as we do Éponine and Azelma!

12:14.340 --> 12:16.530
Yes, thank you.

12:18.350 --> 12:19.450
Be a good girl.

12:19.470 --> 12:20.700
It doesn't hurt.

12:20.730 --> 12:21.410
Cosette.

12:22.060 --> 12:23.040
Yes, Mother!

12:25.060 --> 12:26.210
Come here for a second.

12:26.560 --> 12:27.210
Yes!

12:48.490 --> 12:49.790
Cosette...

12:49.800 --> 12:50.360
Yes?

12:55.010 --> 12:59.870
You will be living here with Monsieur and Madame for a while.

12:59.890 --> 13:01.990
What about you, Mother?

13:02.020 --> 13:09.350
Mother is going to work in a town far away, beyond that road.

13:10.190 --> 13:11.250
I'll go too!

13:15.530 --> 13:17.510
Cosette, I want you to wait for me here.

13:21.620 --> 13:22.850
No!

13:22.870 --> 13:28.400
I want to go with you, Mother!

13:33.590 --> 13:38.240
Cosette, I don't want to leave you, either.

13:40.930 --> 13:49.830
But, I must go alone to find a house where we can live together.

13:51.110 --> 13:52.040
Really?

13:53.820 --> 13:57.470
Mother will be lonely, but I will do my best
to find us a house and come back for you.

13:57.990 --> 14:00.050
Mother will be lonely?

14:00.070 --> 14:05.990
Of course! That's why as soon as I find us a home, I'll come back for you!

14:08.210 --> 14:09.100
Mother...

14:10.750 --> 14:11.900
I will wait.

14:17.510 --> 14:18.400
Cosette...

14:42.450 --> 14:44.260
Mother!

15:12.810 --> 15:14.710
Hey, Cosette, here

15:15.900 --> 15:17.520
You dropped your hat.

15:17.530 --> 15:19.050
Dropped your hat!

15:19.070 --> 15:20.470
Thank you!

15:20.490 --> 15:22.400
Let's go play, Cosette!

15:22.410 --> 15:23.180
Let's play!

15:23.530 --> 15:27.720
Éponine, Azelma, come here. Cosette doesn't have time to play.

15:28.120 --> 15:29.600
Hey, come here!

15:31.290 --> 15:32.730
This is great!

15:33.460 --> 15:37.940
We can pay our debts with this! What a beautiful sound!

15:39.340 --> 15:40.820
Don't dilly-dally!

15:44.300 --> 15:48.490
I'm talking to you, Cosette! Now, go get changed!

15:49.270 --> 15:51.160
If you cry, I'll have you clean the outside of the inn!

15:55.020 --> 15:56.540
Cosette...

15:57.110 --> 15:59.270
My precious Cosette...

16:01.490 --> 16:02.340
Forgive me.

16:04.700 --> 16:07.010
Mother didn't want to leave you.

16:08.200 --> 16:09.970
But, I had no choice.

16:11.000 --> 16:15.060
I will return as soon as possible.

16:16.290 --> 16:19.150
Then, I will never leave you again.

16:20.010 --> 16:24.360
Inside of my heart, there is only you, Cosette.

16:26.050 --> 16:29.370
Cosette, my little Cosette...

16:31.310 --> 16:34.960
Cosette, my precious Cosette.

16:36.350 --> 16:39.970
Montreuil-Sur Mer

16:48.330 --> 16:50.310
You're so lucky to have free time!

16:50.330 --> 16:51.600
I don't really have free time.

16:51.700 --> 16:53.390
Um, excuse me.

16:53.660 --> 16:54.230
Yes?

16:54.960 --> 16:57.940
I hear there is a factory in this town.

16:58.210 --> 17:00.790
Oh, you mean Monsieur Madeleine's factory.

17:00.800 --> 17:02.360
Monsieur Madeleine?

17:02.380 --> 17:08.070
He arrived three years ago and built a black glass factory.

17:08.100 --> 17:14.290
It was a small factory at first, but thanks to Monsieur
Madeleine's business-sense, it quickly flourished!

17:14.310 --> 17:17.040
He's now the mayor of this town!

17:17.150 --> 17:19.920
Are you perhaps looking to work at the factory?

17:20.070 --> 17:20.810
Yes...

17:21.030 --> 17:25.840
He's sure to hire you! He never turns away a poor person!

17:26.110 --> 17:26.630
Hey!

17:26.660 --> 17:28.150
Um, sorry...

17:28.450 --> 17:29.640
No, it's quite all right!

17:29.780 --> 17:33.600
The factory is right past that marketplace.

17:33.910 --> 17:35.430
Yes, thank you!

17:35.460 --> 17:36.560
Thief!

17:36.580 --> 17:38.730
He's a bread thief! Someone capture him!

17:38.750 --> 17:39.650
You little...

17:39.840 --> 17:40.310
Hey!

17:40.590 --> 17:41.650
Stop right there!

17:46.470 --> 17:47.320
What the hell?!

17:48.390 --> 17:50.240
You little punk, I'll kill you!

17:57.560 --> 18:03.380
Monsieur Madeleine! I'm sorry, I got carried away... are you all right?

18:03.570 --> 18:04.770
Yes, I'm fine.

18:05.190 --> 18:06.720
Monsieur Madeleine?

18:07.660 --> 18:11.470
I will take care of this boy, please forgive him, this time.

18:12.790 --> 18:13.760
Return the bread.

18:14.750 --> 18:18.730
That bread isn't yours, return it at once.

18:24.050 --> 18:27.610
I can't refuse a request from Mayor Madeleine himself!

18:28.550 --> 18:29.990
Don't do it again, boy!

18:33.260 --> 18:35.620
You're not from around here, are you? What is your name?

18:36.140 --> 18:37.580
You didn't have to butt in!

18:40.980 --> 18:42.080
What are you doing?!

18:42.440 --> 18:43.130
Come with me!

18:43.520 --> 18:45.670
Let go! That hurts!

18:46.530 --> 18:48.090
That man is...

18:49.860 --> 18:51.090
Mayor Madeleine?

18:52.370 --> 18:56.280
What's the big idea? Did you rescue me just to arrest me?

18:56.700 --> 18:58.180
I'll escape, you know!

18:58.620 --> 19:00.440
I won't let anyone capture me!

19:01.380 --> 19:03.690
What's the big idea?! Say something, you weirdo!

19:04.420 --> 19:05.900
Enter.

19:15.770 --> 19:17.910
Eat, this is for you.

19:22.560 --> 19:25.460
Is your family waiting for you to return?

19:27.070 --> 19:30.720
Do not fret, there's enough for them as well.

19:32.570 --> 19:34.220
Take it with you.

19:48.090 --> 19:51.460
Damn, what's your problem? Why did you have to do something so foolish?!

19:51.970 --> 19:58.300
It wasn't foolish! I cannot leave someone be who commits
a crime to save their family from starvation!

19:59.060 --> 20:00.970
It's the humane thing to do!

20:01.690 --> 20:07.340
However, this is nothing compared to what that man did for me, back then.

20:09.530 --> 20:10.840
<i>Yes...</i>

20:11.400 --> 20:14.800
<i>Long ago, when I went by the name of Jean Valjean...</i>

20:19.040 --> 20:21.240
I see, so you've come from Paris.

20:21.540 --> 20:22.140
Yes...

20:22.160 --> 20:23.690
Are you alone?

20:27.420 --> 20:28.820
Do you have a family?

20:31.960 --> 20:33.040
No...

20:34.720 --> 20:35.740
I see...

20:36.350 --> 20:37.490
You're hired.

20:38.310 --> 20:40.200
Thank you!

20:45.560 --> 20:46.460
What is your name?

20:47.230 --> 20:47.750
Alain...

20:48.070 --> 20:51.920
I see, Alain... I wish to hire you as an errand-runner.

20:53.360 --> 20:55.510
Come back tomorrow, at 8 AM.

20:56.370 --> 20:59.350
What are you saying? I'm not coming back!

21:10.670 --> 21:12.400
What's his problem?

21:13.090 --> 21:15.150
Brother!

21:19.430 --> 21:20.580
It's delicious!

21:20.600 --> 21:21.950
Thank you, Brother!

21:22.390 --> 21:24.830
Take your time eating it, this bread is yours.

21:24.850 --> 21:26.080
Yes!

21:27.150 --> 21:30.080
Alain, I wish to hire you as an errand-runner.

21:31.440 --> 21:32.840
What a weirdo...

21:36.990 --> 21:40.260
<i>Thank goodness, things are starting to look up!</i>

21:41.370 --> 21:46.140
<i>Mother will find a house for us to live in, as soon as possible!</i>

21:47.420 --> 21:48.600
<i>Cosette...</i>

21:49.040 --> 21:50.610
<i>My Cosette...</i>

21:52.420 --> 21:55.490
Work harder! I'm not going to hold back just because you're a child!

21:58.430 --> 22:01.410
You better not leave one speck of garbage lying around!

22:01.640 --> 22:03.950
If you don't do your job, you re not having any supper!

22:06.560 --> 22:07.460
Mother...

22:13.470 --> 22:16.480
ma maman (my mother)

22:17.440 --> 22:20.650
I like you very much, Mother

22:17.440 --> 22:20.650
Daisukiyo nee okaasan

22:21.310 --> 22:24.690
I love you, Mother

22:21.310 --> 22:24.690
Aishiteru nee okaasan

22:25.320 --> 22:29.160
Your warm inviting scent

22:25.320 --> 22:29.160
Atataku ii nioi

22:29.160 --> 22:32.530
My precious mother

22:29.160 --> 22:32.530
Taisetsuna okaasan

22:33.330 --> 22:36.410
As long as you call out to me

22:33.330 --> 22:36.410
Yobikakeru sore dake de

22:37.370 --> 22:40.580
It brings me joy, Mother

22:37.370 --> 22:40.580
Ureshii no nee okaasan

22:41.290 --> 22:45.340
My only mother

22:41.290 --> 22:45.340
Kono sekai ni tatta hitori

22:45.340 --> 22:48.430
in this world

22:45.340 --> 22:48.430
Watashi no okaasan

22:49.760 --> 22:51.640
Hug me tightly

22:49.760 --> 22:51.640
Dakishimete gyutto

22:51.640 --> 22:53.600
Kiss me gently

22:51.640 --> 22:53.600
Kisu wo shitte sotto

22:53.600 --> 23:01.310
Always be by my side

22:53.600 --> 23:01.310
Itsudemo watashi no soba ni ite ne

23:01.810 --> 23:04.570
On the path lined with chestnut trees

23:01.810 --> 23:04.570
Maronie no michi

23:04.570 --> 23:09.530
we walk hand-in-hand

23:04.570 --> 23:09.530
Futari te wo tori aruku

23:09.530 --> 23:13.240
If we sing together,

23:09.530 --> 23:13.240
Isshoni utaeba

23:13.240 --> 23:17.410
we can have fun with just that.

23:13.240 --> 23:17.410
Tanoshii ne sore dake de

23:17.700 --> 23:21.620
Bathing in the sunlight filtering through the canopy

23:17.700 --> 23:21.620
Komorebi no naka yureru

23:21.620 --> 23:25.630
Your beautiful eyes

23:21.620 --> 23:25.630
Kirei na hitomi

23:25.630 --> 23:29.260
And that gentle smile

23:25.630 --> 23:29.260
Yawaraka na hohoemi de

23:29.260 --> 23:34.970
envelop me.

23:29.260 --> 23:34.970
Watashi wo tsutsumu no

23:39.680 --> 24:09.550
Preview

23:41.820 --> 23:46.970
Wow! How terrible! Why does Cosette have to be separated from Fantine?!

23:46.990 --> 23:50.770
To think that a person can't find work just because she has a child...

23:50.790 --> 23:53.650
The period of Les Misérables must have been a rough time.

23:53.670 --> 23:55.270
I can't picture it...

23:55.290 --> 23:56.940
That's what makes it terrible!

23:56.960 --> 24:01.070
Next time on Les Misérables: Jean Valjean's Secret!

